=== [1] dS tail-induced secular inertia drift (Haas-Poisson, q^2 -> G m^2) ===
  Sun          H0 : frac. inertia change per Hubble time = 1.12e-23   (need O(1) for MOND -> deficit 23 orders)
  Sun          H_L: frac. inertia change per Hubble time = 8.97e-24   (need O(1) for MOND -> deficit 23 orders)
  proton       H0 : frac. inertia change per Hubble time = 9.40e-81   (need O(1) for MOND -> deficit 80 orders)
  proton       H_L: frac. inertia change per Hubble time = 7.54e-81   (need O(1) for MOND -> deficit 80 orders)
  1 Msun star  H0 : frac. inertia change per Hubble time = 1.12e-23   (need O(1) for MOND -> deficit 23 orders)
  1 Msun star  H_L: frac. inertia change per Hubble time = 8.97e-24   (need O(1) for MOND -> deficit 23 orders)

=== [2] tail velocity-force scale vs MOND scale (Sun, v=220 km/s) ===
  H0: zeta = 1.12e-23;  |a_self| ~ zeta*H*v = 5.58e-36 m/s^2  vs a0 = 9.36e-11  -> short by 25 orders
  H_L: zeta = 8.97e-24;  |a_self| ~ zeta*H*v = 3.59e-36 m/s^2  vs a0 = 9.36e-11  -> short by 25 orders
  (kinematic 'cosmic dragging' -Hv is universal but is momentum redshift, not a force;
   it is acceleration-blind and already in every GR/Newtonian cosmological calculation.)

=== [3] frequency window of deep-MOND orbits ===
  v =  80 km/s: omega(a=a0) = 1.17e-15 s^-1 =    516 H0   (period 0.17 Gyr)
  v = 150 km/s: omega(a=a0) = 6.24e-16 s^-1 =    275 H0   (period 0.32 Gyr)
  v = 220 km/s: omega(a=a0) = 4.25e-16 s^-1 =    188 H0   (period 0.47 Gyr)
  -> the kernel must deliver O(1) effects at omega ~ (1e2-1e3) H, where dS-IR
     secular enhancements (which live at omega <~ H) do not operate.

=== [4] McCulloch QI high-a tail vs Saturn ===
  H0: delta_a(Saturn) = cH = 6.80e-10 m/s^2 vs Folkner 1e-14 -> x68,009
  H_L: delta_a(Saturn) = cH = 5.46e-10 m/s^2 vs Folkner 1e-14 -> x54,561
  (g_N(Saturn) = 6.460e-05 m/s^2; same arithmetic class as F1's x54,000 kill.)

