=== [6] massive-kernel crossover scale ===
  a/cH =   0.100: kappa/H =   1.005;  m_phi=hbar H/c^2 exponent m/kappa = 0.995
  a/cH =   1.000: kappa/H =   1.414;  m_phi=hbar H/c^2 exponent m/kappa = 0.707
  a/cH =   5.789: kappa/H =   5.875;  m_phi=hbar H/c^2 exponent m/kappa = 0.170
  a/cH = 100.000: kappa/H = 100.005;  m_phi=hbar H/c^2 exponent m/kappa = 0.010
  -> for m_phi ~ H the Boltzmann/Takagi suppression turns on exactly around a ~ cH:
     the only known kernel class whose natural crossover sits at the MOND scale.
